.TH LBM_BENCH 1 "October 2026" "wind-tunnel-2d" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lbm_bench \- headless validator for the Schaefer-Turek 2D-2 cylinder benchmark
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lbm_bench
.RI [ res "...] [" steps=N ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lbm_bench
is the headless validator. No window, no sliders, only numbers. It
implements the Schaefer-Turek 2D-2 laminar-cylinder benchmark (channel
2.2 m by 0.41 m, cylinder D = 0.1 m deliberately 0.005 m off-axis, Re =
100) with the full validated solver stack:
.IP \[bu] 2
TRT collision (omega_p from viscosity, omega_m from the magic parameter
Lambda = 3/16, decoupling the wall location from viscosity);
.IP \[bu]
Bouzidi interpolated bounce-back with analytic q-fractions against the
exact circle (2nd-order curved wall);
.IP \[bu]
Guo non-equilibrium-extrapolation in/outflow (2nd-order BCs);
.IP \[bu]
q-consistent Mei-Luo-Shyy momentum exchange for Cd and Cl;
.IP \[bu]
Welch-windowed FFT (sample floor + window cross-check) for Strouhal.
.PP
Reference values at Re = 100: St = 0.295-0.305, Cd = 3.22-3.24, Cl_amp
= 1.0.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.IR res "..."
One or more resolution values (nodes across the cylinder diameter).
Common ladder:
.BR "20 40 80" .
.TP
.BR steps=N
Explicit step chunk size for a single call. Useful under short call
limits; see
.B CHECKPOINTING
below. Default: run until the gate is satisfied.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LB_VERBOSE=1
Print per-chunk progress (step count, period estimate, gate state).
.TP
.B LB_RESULTS=path
Persist each resolution's final (res, nx, ny, Re, St, Cd, Cl) to a file
for later assembly.
.TP
.B LB_ASSEMBLE=1
With
.BR LB_RESULTS ,
print the assembled convergence table on exit; with three or more
resolutions, print a Richardson extrapolation (
.IR f_ext ,
error bar, observed order
.IR p )
across the three finest, with non-monotone series explicitly flagged.
.SH CHECKPOINTING
State dumps to
.BI /tmp/lbm_ckpt_ res .bin
after each chunk and resumes next call. Delete the file to restart that
resolution. This exists for sandboxes with short call limits; on normal
hardware you launch
.B lbm_bench
once and wait.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Standard convergence ladder:
.PP
.RS
.B ./lbm_bench 20 40
.RE
.PP
Three-resolution ladder with persistence, then Richardson:
.PP
.RS
.B LB_RESULTS=conv.txt ./lbm_bench 20 40 80
.br
.B LB_ASSEMBLE=1 LB_RESULTS=conv.txt ./lbm_bench 20
.RE
.PP
Resume a long res=80 run across short calls:
.PP
.RS
.B rm /tmp/lbm_ckpt_80.bin   # start fresh
.br
.B ./lbm_bench 80 steps=5000
.br
.B ./lbm_bench 80 steps=5000   # resumes until the gate fires
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.BI /tmp/lbm_ckpt_ res .bin
Checkpoint file. Safe to delete.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wind_tunnel (1),
.BR lbm_tunnel (1),
.BR lbm_pro (1)
.SH NOTES
Validation measurements at res = 40 on the project author's machine (6
threads):
.B St = 0.3017, Cd = 3.215, Cl_amp = 1.008,
within 1% of reference on all three; |dSt| 20->40 = 0.49%.
